    {
      "id": "1555793260763549808",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-03T04:06:58.607+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Hey all, I was running the machine and was asked to post a little vid. I'll post more in the near future. I have a few I want to finish quickly, then do some small upgrades (better lighting and some small things)\nCurrently picking some @BreakingTaps dies. \nBasic setup is \n- robot arm\n- cartesian bot below wafer that pushes die off tape\n- other misc boards that power solenoids, or lights, or motors and a game controller\nAll the boards are networked over canbus\n\nHUD is cpython bridged onto bus as well. All control is handled through a web interface (Starlette)\n- up camera finds die on nozzle\n- feeder_camera locates the pocket -- place happens between offsets from these\n- down camera is on arm, does mostly calibration and location of the wafer (the dicing house sticks them on there all willy nilly, it's bad)\n\nLike I said, more coming soon, feel free to ask questions",
      "author": {
        "id": "756011607603019777",
        "name": "anfroholic",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "Andrew Wingate",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [
          {
